    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-064 — Scroll height regression fix.** Restores Wikipedia scrollbar.\n\n**Production-verified 2026-11-03**: scrollbar appears, wheel scroll works, bottom of article reachable.\n\n## The regression\n\nADR-057's `html { height: 100% }` clamp broke page scroll. Wikipedia's CSS reset includes `html, body { height: 100% }`. Before ADR-057, `%` height was skipped → `<html>` box = content height. After ADR-057, `html { height: 100% }` resolves against `viewport_h` → `<html>` box = 678px (viewport) even with 30,000+px of content below.\n\n`sync_drawing_area_size` then set the DrawingArea to 678px. ScrolledWindow saw \"content = viewport\" → no scroll range → no scrollbar.\n\n## The fix\n\n`layout_height()` walks the Box tree iteratively for the deepest `y + height`. Box-only traversal: Inline fragments bounded by their parent Box.\n\n## Verified (screenshots 2026-11-03)\n\n- Scrollbar visible on Wikipedia right edge\n- Wheel scroll works\n- Can reach references/footer at bottom\n\n## Extra relayout cost\n\nPage load now shows 5 PERF-CASCADE lines (was 4). The taller DrawingArea triggers one more GTK layout cycle. Extra relayout at ~533ms is known cost, not regression.\n\n## Test count\n\n687 / 2627 unchanged.\n\n## Verification category\n\nProduction-visual, user-reported.\n\nRefs #268\n",
